A||N||26||Monkeyman||AUSFIERO UPDATE||||4||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||07-14-2001||09:57 AM||||I received an email from Aus' wife this morning.  Since I have no idea how to post the email here, I'll have to translate.<P>Jim had surgery Friday (as most of you know) and by Friday evening, he was awake, in very little pain and feeling none of the symptoms that mandated the surgery in the 1<sup>st</sup> place.  The only complication thus far seems to be the inability to swallow solid foods (I'll bet it's from the anesthesia intubation).  He was walking (shakily) by Saturday morning and hopes to be out by the 17<sup>th</sup> of this month.  Jims' doctors are amazed at the speed of his recovery.  He said to thank everyone for their prayers and support.  Hopefully, he'll be 100% within a month, but Jim feels that his recovery should come much sooner if the past couple of days are any indication.  <P>Aus' wife isn't really into computers so if anyone would like to send him an email, perhaps (at least until he gets home) you could send it to me and I'd be happy to forward it to him whenever his wife feels up to it.  I plan on keeping in contact with both Jim and his wife.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||4
Z||000001||Hartz||07-14-2001||10:26 AM||||Great news.  Tell him not to push it and take it easy!  We'll keep him in our thoughts.<P>Hartz<BR>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo||||reg||10
Z||000002||Raydar||07-14-2001||10:59 AM||||Yes, <BR>That is great news. Thanks!<P>Raydar||||reg||14
Z||000003||Cliff Pennock||07-14-2001||11:18 AM||||Tell him to fake not being able to walk. Why? Two words: Spunge baths.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>(for best results: make sure you have a female nurse)||||reg||1
Z||000004||Steve Normington||07-14-2001||12:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cliff Pennock:<BR><B>Tell him to fake not being able to walk. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If they think you have trouble walking, then they are going to catherize you.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> That takes all of the fun out of the sponge bath.||||reg||1
Z||000005||grinthock||07-14-2001||12:05 PM||||My Father-in-law was in the hospital for 8 months with compilcations from the same kinda of surgury, I am very glad to hear all this stuff, Jim is such a great guy, my prayers are still flowing along for him... Take it easy dude, do'nt push it!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Monkeyman||07-14-2001||12:51 PM||||Guys--I'll pass along the well wishes to him this evening in my daily email.<P>Cliff--Jim and I already discussed the nurse/sponge bath idea.  Great minds think alike!<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
